image-to-pixel-art (Rust)
=========================

Provenance
----------

This crate is a Rust port of the portable TypeScript library:

  https://github.com/sherotree/image-to-pixel-art

That library packages the core pixel-processing behavior demonstrated by the
browser tool at:

  https://www.uwarp.design/image-to-pixel-art

That tool’s algorithm and palette helpers originated as a TypeScript port of
Pixel It; the TypeScript repository is the standalone open-source form of that
core (pipeline order: pixelate → grayscale → palette → max size). This Rust
crate ports the same core buffer algorithms for crates.io consumers.

Upstream algorithm
------------------

The pixelation / grayscale / palette matching algorithm is a port of:

  https://github.com/giventofly/pixelit
  Author: José Moreira
  License: MIT (see LICENSE)

Built-in named palettes (Vinik24, Sunset 8, NES, Endesga 16, …) are included
for API parity with the reference tool UI / TypeScript library.

